  "open_work": [
    "Eleven immutable source records remain as retirement boundaries and hidden native comparison stock. The source author explicitly describes wet cells in glass jars wired in series; this fitting adds passive physical forms only.",
    "ADAPTATION: native inspection found 1595 genuine triangle pairs intersecting the retained repair cabinet. The fitted charging assembly is translated in source X only: its left edge is derived from the authored counter_top right edge plus 0.15m. All original Y positions, heights, relative jar spacing and maxima remain. The cabinet, original layout and every other fitting are unchanged; no context intersection is waived.",
    "ADAPTATION: an open floor-supported timber rack replaces the solid body. Five seated wooden pads bridge the original 50mm jar gap without raising the original 0.89m rack worktop.",
    "ADAPTATION: finite hollow elliptical glass jars retain literal source colour/alpha, roughness and normal maps. Passive neutral opaque fill and untyped plate stock make the source wet-cell display legible without specifying chemistry, capacity, charging rate, current or safe operation.",
    "ADAPTATION: narrow jar mouths and inserted cap collars bridge the source 10mm jar/cap gap. Caps and two passive terminals per jar stay below the original 1.33m cap maximum; four seated copper display links follow the source series description. No lead route, utility supply, powered circuit, signal, interaction or carrier change is inferred.",
    "Original room, walls, door/handle, cabinet, accepted native bench/apparatus/valve rack, other stock, keys, saves, hours and services retain their owners. No new map, material key, shared shader, lettering or architecture cutout.",
    "Positive connected stock, source/context clearance, actual floor/jar/cap/link bearings, strict metric charts, rendered review, normal mounting and reconstruction remain to be verified. This ignored preparation grants no proof or acceptance."
